1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,840
I had a gentleman who came six plus months ago.

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,880
I'll take it some months earlier, came out here,

3
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:05,080
took time away from the business,

4
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:07,160
and finally gets his chance to have a question.

5
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:08,520
And he says, hey, Alex, can you go through

6
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:09,640
the Closer framework?

7
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:11,360
And I said, before I answer the question,

8
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:12,640
can you tell me what Closer rate is?

9
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,200
And he says, 40%.

10
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,400
So you went through all of that

11
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,640
to have this one opportunity to have an answer

12
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:20,880
that in no way will change your business.

13
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:22,320
A lot of times, us as entrepreneurs,

14
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:24,600
we will focus on the thing that we enjoy the most

15
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,400
rather than the thing that the business needs the most.

16
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,880
And typically the thing the business needs the most

17
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:29,360
is not the thing that you're the best at.

18
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:30,720
A lot of times, art efficiencies

19
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:32,600
translate into the business efficiencies.

20
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,560
And you can be unbalanced as an entrepreneur,

21
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:35,680
but the business can't be.

22
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:36,760
You will always be constrained

23
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:38,240
by whatever the weak link is in the business,

24
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:39,480
and that's fundamentally the whole point

25
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:40,880
of the theory of constraints.

